From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller 999999: every self-attributing handler leaves the author in cmdu->origin

99994 built the mechanism: a handler that discovers `origin` was only the
relay corrects cmdu->origin, and the dispatch tail resolves the author
once for every mapc_sync_*() write and for node expiry. It rolled it out
to one handler - Topology Response. The blind review of 2026-08-04
(finding 1.3/1.15) counted the rest: any CMDU that arrives through a
1905 relay is still persisted under the relay.

Roll the idiom out to the remaining self-attributing handlers:

  - handle_topology_notification: the AL MAC TLV names the author
    outright; the handler already rebinds its local n and forgot to tell
    the caller. This is the roaming path - a client association event
    persisted under the relay is why the DB shows the wrong owner for
    minutes after a roam when the event crossed a hop.

  - handle_ap_caps_report: no TLV names an AL address, but every radio
    TLV names a radio and a radio belongs to exactly one node; rebind to
    the owner of the first named radio.

  - handle_ap_metrics_response: same through the BSSID every AP Metrics
    TLV names. Rebinding n here also fixes n->est_thput_dl bookkeeping,
    which was charged to the relay.

The pattern is one lookup at the top of the handler, no behaviour change
when the frame arrived directly (owner == n).

Verify on hardware, mesh chained controller <- 8g <- x8: roam a client
between 8g and x8 and watch "is from ... relayed by ..." in the
controller log for CMDU 0x0001 (notification), then sta.agent_almac in
mapc.db - it must name the node the client actually sits on, within
seconds, even when the event crossed two hops.
--- a/src/cntlr_map.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_map.c
@@ -204,6 +204,14 @@
 		return -1;
 	}
 
+	/* The AL MAC TLV names the author. Correcting our local n is not
+	 * enough (the 99994 lesson): the caller persists the node it
+	 * resolved from the frame source, so leave the author where the
+	 * caller reads it back. Roaming lives here - the client association
+	 * event must be persisted under the agent that saw it, not under
+	 * the relay it arrived through. */
+	memcpy(cmdu->origin, almacaddr, 6);
+
 	if (!map_cmdu_validate_parse(cmdu, tv, ARRAY_SIZE(tv), n->map_profile)) {
 		warn("%s: map_cmdu_validate_parse failed,  err = (%d) '%s'\n",
 		     __func__, map_error, map_strerror(map_error));
@@ -1890,6 +1898,23 @@
 	 *  debug_ap_caps_report() does this.
 	 */
 
+	/* No TLV here names the author by AL address, but every radio TLV
+	 * names a radio and a radio belongs to exactly one node. When the
+	 * frame came through a relay, n is the relay: rebind to the radio
+	 * owner and leave it in cmdu->origin for the caller (99994 idiom). */
+	if (tv[AP_CAPABILITY_REPORT_AP_RADIO_BASIC_CAPS_IDX][0]) {
+		uint8_t *ruid =
+			(uint8_t *)tv[AP_CAPABILITY_REPORT_AP_RADIO_BASIC_CAPS_IDX][0]->data;
+		struct netif_radio *nr = cntlr_find_radio(c, ruid);
+
+		if (nr && nr->agent && nr->agent != n) {
+			dbg("%s: AP Caps Report is about " MACFMT ", relayed by " MACFMT "\n",
+			    __func__, MAC2STR(nr->agent->almacaddr), MAC2STR(n->almacaddr));
+			n = nr->agent;
+			memcpy(cmdu->origin, n->almacaddr, 6);
+		}
+	}
+
 	/* AP Capability TLV */
 	if (tv[AP_CAPABILITY_REPORT_AP_CAPABILITY_IDX][0]) {
 		struct tlv_ap_cap *p =
@@ -2434,6 +2459,21 @@
 		return -1;
 	}
 
+	/* Same relay problem, resolved through the BSSID every AP Metrics
+	 * TLV names: a BSS belongs to exactly one node. Rebinding n also
+	 * fixes the per-node est_thput bookkeeping below. */
+	if (tv[0][0]) {
+		struct tlv_ap_metrics *p0 = (struct tlv_ap_metrics *)tv[0][0]->data;
+		struct netif_iface *bss0 = cntlr_find_bss(c, p0->bssid);
+
+		if (bss0 && bss0->agent && bss0->agent != n) {
+			dbg("%s: AP Metrics Response is about " MACFMT ", relayed by " MACFMT "\n",
+			    __func__, MAC2STR(bss0->agent->almacaddr), MAC2STR(n->almacaddr));
+			n = bss0->agent;
+			memcpy(cmdu->origin, n->almacaddr, 6);
+		}
+	}
+
 	/* AP Metrics TLV */
 	idx = 0;
 	while (idx < TLV_MAXNUM && tv[0][idx]) {
